/-!
SE. `Module.support` is defined by nonzero prime localizations, precisely the
stalk support of the associated sheaf. Hartshorne coherence is used only over
Noetherian rings/schemes; no coherence convention is changed here.
SE-1/3/4 use the topological zero-neighborhood criterion, kernel computation,
and stalk exactness below. No global extension-by-zero functor is constructed.
SE-7 checks radical containment versus an ideal power and clearing finitely
many denominators; the identification with the sheaf kernel is by the affine
basis in the prose. SE-8's finite numerators, finite sum and local span
interfaces check the affine enlargement; gluing that enlargement with the
original coherent subsheaf and the finite induction over X are not packaged
as a theorem of coherent sheaves. SE-11 uses residue fiber rank, not fraction
field rank: `fiberRankFormula` records the comparison. Its critical reduced
kernel argument is proved below. The assembly of these local surjections into openness of the fiber-rank
loci and the full sheaf equivalence remain interface assembly gaps.
SE-12's existing proof is covered by ii-5-exe.lean and module-algebra.lean.
-/
